From b85797ed232e207934e332ab816d050c1b020362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@do-not-panic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:00:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Give the player orientation a defined value on init

CControl::Init() left corientation untouched, so the first physics
step of a race read whatever the previous race left there: the
orientation is only recomputed by AdjustOrientation at the end of the
step, and an airborne paddle force during that step is rotated by it.
The racer starts a hair above the surface and therefore counts as
airborne on the first step, so a paddle held at the start produced a
different force depending on the race that ran before. Compute the
initial orientation from the course normal and the initial velocity,
the same construction AdjustOrientation uses on the ground, so a race
no longer depends on the process history.

Found with the headless bridge: replaying a recorded action trace in a
fresh process and after another race diverged from the first tick.

Signed-off-by: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@do-not-panic.com>
---
 src/physics.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/physics.cpp b/src/physics.cpp
index a7dd143..aa41611 100644
--- a/src/physics.cpp
+++ b/src/physics.cpp
@@ -92,6 +92,17 @@ void CControl::Init() {
 	collisions = 0;
 	colliding = false;
 
+	// Give the orientation a defined value. The first physics step can
+	// read it (an airborne paddle is rotated by it) before
+	// AdjustOrientation runs, and it otherwise carries the previous
+	// race's final orientation into the new one.
+	TVector3d init_z = -nml;
+	TVector3d init_y = ProjectToPlane(nml, init_vel);
+	init_y.Norm();
+	TVector3d init_x = CrossProduct(init_y, init_z);
+	TMatrix<4, 4> cob_mat(init_x, init_y, init_z);
+	corientation = MakeQuaternionFromMatrix(cob_mat);
+
 	// tricks
 	front_flip = false;
 	back_flip = false;
